WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.567
-It's so nice to see you.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.601
You've been on the show a bunch
of times separately.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:07.367
The first time together.
-That's right.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:08.767
-What better way
to start your season?

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:11.000
-Mother and daughter, yes.
You both look great.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.767
Welcome, and thanks for being
here. Appreciate it.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:15.300
How are the grandkids?
-They are so great.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.367
-Three now right, Chelsea?
-Three.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.868
Seven, six, and three. Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.534
-And we had the best summer.
How was your summer?

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:24.033
-It was unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:26.267
-Very, very lucky.
We're just happy and good.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.501
And the kids are great.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:30.334
I know you spoil your kids --
your grandkids.

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:32.801
-Just a little.
-She does, Jimmy.

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:35.100
Then ask did she spoil me?

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:39.334
-She did. She did.
-Did she? She didn't.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.300
-No, no, it skips a generation.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:45.133
-Is that how it works?
-Yeah, yeah, you're supposed to

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.467
both spoil
and be kind of subversive.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.934
-Yeah, I understand.
-Like, do you need to have

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.934
ice cream three times a day?
-Yeah.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:55.868
That's what a good grandma does.
-I want happy grandchildren.

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:58.934
-Even with bribery.
-Even with bribery.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:03.234
And then, you know, Chelsea
limits screen time,

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.067
which I think is right.
It's absolutely right.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:07.133
-But do you limit screen time?
-Well...

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.601
I just feel like there's
so much they can learn.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:14.534
-That's exactly right.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:17.767
-I go for a run, and my mom's
like, "Just one video."

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.767
And I'm like, "Okay."
And I come back from my run

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.367
like an hour later,
and she's like,

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:24.200
"So, we're on the 17th
volcano explosion."

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.300
And I was like,
"Did we need the last 15?"

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.334
-They've really seen a lot of
volcano explosions.

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.701
They can learn a lot.
-And the megalodon.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.501
The gigantic prehistoric shark.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:36.567
There are so many great videos
to see.

00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:39.767
-I just can't stop.
-I'm happy that you're here.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:42.467
I want to talk to you about
your show on Apple TV+, "Gutsy."

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.100
But I wanted to ask you both,
since you both

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.501
lived at the White House.
-Yes, we did.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.100
-Yes.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.434
How easy is it to walk out with
boxes of classified documents?

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:59.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:02.300
-It's the plural that kills me,
right?

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.968
You're like not just
one box or one document --

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:08.701
boxes and thousands of
documents.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.968
-Does he know what he's doing?

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.567
What would you do with that?

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:16.667
I mean, is it for -- is it
for the presidential library?

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:22.100
-Well, usually when it comes to
presidential libraries,

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.000
everything is in the archives.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.234
We have a National Archive
and Record Administration

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.968
where everything goes.

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:33.968
And then it gets transferred to
a presidential library.

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:36.067
At least that's the way
it used to happen.

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:38.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.467
-Now he's got his own stash
in his basement.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.667
-Yeah, I guess.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:47.200
I mean, that's what
we're finding out.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.000
-I also wanted to ask you --
I got the opportunity,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.300
honored to talk to the president
of Ukraine, President Zelenskyy.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.067
And as Secretary of State,

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.033
I know you've been to Ukraine
many times.

00:02:58.033 --> 00:03:00.534
What are the next steps
for Ukraine?

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:06.367
-Well, look, I am thrilled that
they have gotten the support

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.901
and solidarity of
so much of the world.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.400
Obviously, Europe,
the United States, Canada,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.133
but Japan, other places.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:16.534
They're getting the weapons
they need to defend themselves,

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.868
and they're now on offense.

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:22.901
And I think we have to keep
supporting them, helping them.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:29.267
They were attacked by
an unprovoked act of war,

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:32.200
and they've held out
and they've done better

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.634
than anybody could have
predicted.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.501
And Zelenskyy has been
a true wartime leader.

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.300
I'm so impressed with him.
-Absolutely.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.934
-And I think, you know,
the United States should stand

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:44.267
with him along with all of our
other friends around the world.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:47.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.801
-I agree.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.501
Let's talk about "Gutsy."

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:55.467
"Gutsy" is a docuseries based on
your best-selling book.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.133
-Yes.
-"The Book of Gutsy Women."

00:03:58.133 --> 00:03:59.868
-Right.
-When you did that book,

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.767
which of course we have
at the house,

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.133
did you think, "Oh, we can make
a show out of this?"

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.701
-No. No.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.234
-It was just a continuation of a
conversation we had been having

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:12.100
my whole life of stories
that have inspired us

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.400
that we wanted to share, stories
we were starting to share

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.534
with the grandchildren.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:19.067
Thankfully, she gives them
a diet of inspiration

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:22.601
along with the third bowl of
chocolate chip ice cream.

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:25.033
And then we had the chance
to turn it into a series.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.434
And it was just such a joy.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.667
-It's been so much fun.
-So much fun.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.601
-You guys are obviously
fantastic together,

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:32.534
but I don't know if many get to
see this side of you guys

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:35.000
as mother/daughter
and almost like a comedy team

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.300
when you're talking.
You both go at it.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.467
-I mean, there's just so much
to make fun of.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:43.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:46.534
-She has never stopped.
Literally.

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:48.701
I remember --
-It's my --

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:52.734
-She's a pretty good "put you
in your place" kind of person.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:55.767
-With love.
-With love, yeah, sure.

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:59.934
She was like three or four,
and I say to her, you know,

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.400
I think I should
as her mother, I say,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.868
"You know, Chelsea,
it's cold outside.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.701
You should wear
a sweater or jacket."

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:06.234
She goes, "I don't want to."

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.901
I said, "Well, I know,
but it's cold."

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.467
She goes, "Mom, if you're cold,
wear a sweater or a jacket."

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:13.868
-That's a great line!

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:15.868
"Hey, if you're cold, wear one."

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.701
-So that kind of runs
through the series.

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:22.267
-It's very funny.
-She makes a lot of fun of me.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:23.501
-It's very good.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:25.067
But also you know
what you're doing, too.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:28.334
It's so good, but also
I love that you interview people

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.734
like Megan Thee Stallion.

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:33.567
And then you interview women
like Jane Goodall.

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:36.601
-Yes.
-And you go, "Oh, two women of

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:38.300
two different things,
both powerful,

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.067
both inspiring
in different ways."

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.501
I love that you did that
and you do that.

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:46.734
Also you take some chances on
this docuseries from what I saw,

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.767
especially Chelsea.
-Yes.

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:51.067
-You're like rappelling down
a mountain

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:53.000
and training with the FDNY.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.200
-I mean, okay, I can't quite
call it training.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.934
I mean, I put on the gear
and I tried.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.267
[ Laughter ]
-I think just putting on

00:05:58.267 --> 00:06:01.968
the gear and walking up stairs
is training.

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:04.067
-I was trying to haul that hose.

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:06.868
It was really humbling
and I feel like gratitude is

00:06:06.868 --> 00:06:09.534
an insufficient word
for how in awe I am

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:11.067
of our women of the FDNY.

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:13.000
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.033
You get to see it.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:17.467
You take it for granted,
you know?

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:21.868
Is there a certain person that
you had on the show that you go,

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:24.300
"I want to make sure this person
gets a chance to say something"?

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.033
-Oh, there were so many of them.

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:29.367
And partly, Jimmy, because,
you know,

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:30.834
a lot of them we didn't know.

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:34.300
We might have known of them,
but we had never met them.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:39.067
And I'll just give you a quick
recap of --

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:43.067
We actually met a woman who used
to be a white supremacist

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:48.767
and got out of that life and now
tries to deprogram others.

00:06:48.767 --> 00:06:51.667
And she takes them into nature,
so we went down to Georgia.

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:54.200
We went canoeing on a river
together.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.000
And she talked about
her life journey.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.234
And there was a young woman
with her whose last name

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:04.234
we didn't use because she had
just come out of that movement

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:06.467
of hate and violence.
-And testified against

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:10.167
some of the worst neo-Nazi
white supremacists.

00:07:10.167 --> 00:07:14.400
-So you're with these women
and you find common ground,

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.634
even though their experiences
are very different.

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:20.601
And then the next thing I did
was to interview two women

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:24.200
who had lost their children
to hate crimes.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.634
One was the mother of
Heather Heyer,

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:28.601
who was murdered
in Charlottesville,

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:31.601
and the other was a black woman.

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:35.601
Her son had just been admitted,
got his commission

00:07:35.601 --> 00:07:38.367
in our military after being in
ROTC, was standing,

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:41.801
minding his own business
and somebody yelling

00:07:41.801 --> 00:07:44.267
racial epithets
stabbed him to death.

00:07:44.267 --> 00:07:47.167
And talking to these women
who'd experienced

00:07:47.167 --> 00:07:50.067
about the worst thing you could
from this kind of hate,

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:55.367
that sadly, unfortunately, is
too much in our lives today,

00:07:55.367 --> 00:08:00.601
they were so amazing in how they
were talking about they had to

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:04.868
get through their grief and
their hatred and their outrage

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:06.701
so that they could continue with
their lives

00:08:06.701 --> 00:08:08.534
and try to do something to help
other people.

00:08:08.534 --> 00:08:10.834
So it goes from the funny --

00:08:10.834 --> 00:08:14.133
We went to Paris
and went to the clown school

00:08:14.133 --> 00:08:16.100
and put on the red noses
and the whole deal --

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.167
all the way to Syria.

00:08:17.167 --> 00:08:18.567
-We're secretly coming
for your job.

00:08:18.567 --> 00:08:21.033
-I know.
I can tell, every appearance.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.400
-I want to see you
with the red nose.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:26.801
-Everyone knows I'm a clown.
I want to show a clip.

00:08:26.801 --> 00:08:28.968
Here's Hillary
and Chelsea Clinton in "Gutsy."

00:08:28.968 --> 00:08:31.934
Take a look at this.
-Going back to Arkansas helps us

00:08:31.934 --> 00:08:34.901
really think through
some of these questions about

00:08:34.901 --> 00:08:36.767
"What does gutsiness
really mean?

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:39.234
How do you make
difficult choices?

00:08:39.234 --> 00:08:42.968
How do you take a leap, a leap
of faith sometimes that you have

00:08:42.968 --> 00:08:44.868
no idea what the outcome is
going to be?"

00:08:44.868 --> 00:08:46.868
Going back is something
I'm looking forward to.

00:08:46.868 --> 00:08:49.434
-Me too.

00:08:49.434 --> 00:08:51.200
-I don't know if you're going to
get much more in there.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.601
You'll be surprised.

00:08:52.601 --> 00:08:54.667
That's very expandable.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.734
Oh, yeah, I got lots of room.

00:08:56.734 --> 00:08:58.067
-Ready to sit on your suitcase?

00:08:58.067 --> 00:08:59.334
-No, I don't need --

00:08:59.334 --> 00:09:01.534
It's very...reliable.
-I know.

00:09:01.534 --> 00:09:03.234
You're very loyal to
that suitcase.

00:09:03.234 --> 00:09:04.601
-I am.

00:09:04.601 --> 00:09:06.734
[ Thunk ]
-Oh, good Lord. Alright.

00:09:06.734 --> 00:09:08.400
-Okay, we're done!

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.167
Let's head to Arkansas!

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:12.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:14.434
-Sit on it?

00:09:14.434 --> 00:09:16.434
Hillary and Chelsea Clinton,
everyone.

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:19.567
"Gutsy" premieres this Friday
on Apple TV+.

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:21.868
When we come back, Hillary and
Chelsea are going head-to-head

00:09:21.868 --> 00:09:23.968
in the Mother Daughter
Challenge. Stick around.

